## Why This Is Asked
Assesses cost-aware design of privacy-preserving observability with edge processing, cross-region deployment, and go/no-go decisions.

## Key Concepts
- Edge compute budgeting
- Privacy-first telemetry
- Data retention and regional regulations
- Multi-region cost models
- Rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function cba(params) {
  // simple cost model
  const deviceCost = params.deviceCPU * 0.1 + params.deviceMem * 0.05;
  const deltaCost = (params.deltaKB / 1024) * 0.02;
  const centralCost = params.retentionMonths * 1000 * 0.01;
  return deviceCost + deltaCost + centralCost;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for GDPR/CCPA across regions?
- What metrics would tie cost to business value beyond raw savings?

## Why This Is Asked
Privacy-preserving on-device experiments enable rapid iteration without raw data leaving devices, aligning with regulatory scrutiny and low-latency user experience goals.

## Key Concepts
- On-device flag evaluation and cohort management
- Local storage and memory budgeting
- Delta-based telemetry with minimal data exposure
- Safe rollout, rollback, and veto mechanisms
- Compliance and auditability considerations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Local flag evaluation snippet (pseudo)
function evalFlag(user, flagRepo) {
  const cohort = user.cohortId;
  const flag = flagRepo.getFlag(cohort);
  return flag.evaluate(user);
}
```

